,\n  "snippet": "import socket\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\nServer module to handle server operations.\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\nThis module provides functionalities to start and manage the server operations.\\r\\r\\nIt utilizes utilities from the utils module.\\r\\r\\n\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\ndef run():\\r\\r\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n    Start the server.\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    This function initiates the server operations by binding to a port\\r\\r\\n    and listening for incoming connections.\\r\\r\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n    # Create a TCP/IP socket\\r\\r\\n    server_socket = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    # Bind the socket to the port\\r\\r\\n    server_address = (\'localhost\', 8080)\\r\\r\\n    print(f\'Starting up on {server_address[0]} port {server_address[1]}\')\\r\\r\\n    server_socket.bind(server_address)\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    # Listen for incoming connections\\r\\r\\n    server_socket.listen(1)\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    while True:\\r\\r\\n        # Wait for a connection\\r\\r\\n        print(\'Waiting for a connection\')\\r\\r\\n        connection, client_address = server_socket.accept()\\r\\r\\n        try:\\r\\r\\n            print(f\'Connection from {client_address}\')\\r\\r\\n            # Receive the data in small chunks and retransmit it\\r\\r\\n            while True:\\r\\r\\n                data = connection.recv(16)\\r\\r\\n                print(f\'Received {data}\')\\r\\r\\n                if data:\\r\\r\\n                    print(\'Sending data back to the client\')\\r\\r\\n                    connection.sendall(data)\\r\\r\\n                else:\\r\\r\\n                    print(\'No more data from\', client_address)\\r\\r\\n                    break\\r\\r\\n        finally:\\r\\r\\n            # Clean up the connection\\r\\r\\n            connection.close()\\r\\r\\n",\n  "truncated": false,\n  "file_size": 1529,\n  "modified_ts": 1780226757.0452435,\n  "mode": "line_range"\n}', 'output': "The `server.py` file is fully loaded. Here's a summary of its contents:\n\n### Overview of `server.py`\n\n- **Modules**:\n  - Imports the `socket` module.\n  \n- **Documentation**:\n  - Contains a docstring explaining that the module is responsible for handling server operations, primarily starting and managing server operations.\n\n- **Functions**:\n  - `run()`: \n    - Starts the server by creating a TCP/IP socket.\n    - Binds the socket to `localhost` on port `8080`.\n    - Listens for incoming connections and accepts them.\n    - Receives data from the client and sends it back.\n\n### Suggestions for Improvement\n\n1. **Exception Handling**:\n   - Enhance error handling, especially around network operations to manage connection errors or socket exceptions.\n\n2. **Documentation**:\n   - Ensure all methods are documented with parameters and return types for better clarity.\n\n3. **Code Improvement**:\n   - Consider refactoring the infinite loop to include a clean server shutdown process.\n\nLet's proceed with the improvements.", 'input_size': 5472, 'output_size': 1018, 'has_tool_calls': True, 'stage': 'after'} 
